From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:33:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] settings_ui: the jail's restart notice has a Restart Agent
 button

Operator ask of 2026-11-23 (item 9): the Agent Sandbox page says "Restart
the agent to apply." once a setting changed, and gave no way to do it -- the
operator had to find each thread and click its lock. The notice now has a
Restart Agent button beside it.

settings_ui does not depend on agent_ui, so the page cannot reach the
threads. agent_sandbox::restart_request carries the ask: the button sets the
JailRestartRequest global (the project root and a growing serial), and every
ConversationView observes it. A view restarts when the request names its
project, its agent's launch record has drifted from the settings of now, and
the serial is one it has not acted on (restart_wanted). It restarts the way
its lock does (ThreadView::restart_agent_for_jail, now pub(crate)): the
transcript is carried, and a turn in progress asks "Restart the agent?"
first. The call is deferred, because the restart updates the view the
observer is running in. Several views of one agent are safe:
restart_connection returns the connection already restarting. Native
threads have no launch record and are left alone.

Logs: agent_sandbox event=restart_requested source=settings serial=N on the
click, agent_sandbox event=restart_for_jail source=settings serial=N per
view that restarts.

Tests: agent_sandbox restart_request_tests.rs (the rule; observers see each
request with a growing serial) and agent_ui
conversation_view/tests/settings_restart_tests.rs (a drifted agent of the
project restarts, another project's request and a view with no launch record
leave it alone). Lab 2026-11-24: 85/85 with the agent_jail tests. Red not
run as a separate step: without the observer the drifted view keeps its
thread, which the assert_ne names.
---

